+--
+-- The panel changes refresh by stretching the vertical front porch at a
+-- constant pixel clock, which is how the stock 60Hz mode is built out of
+-- the 120Hz one. dynamic_modegen below does the same for rates the kernel
+-- does not expose, so the Steam refresh slider behaves like the Deck's.
+-- It is analytic and derives everything from the base mode, so it follows
+-- whichever timings the panel actually reports.
+--
+-- This needs the kernel to push the new porch to the panel controller --
+-- see kernel patch 0138, which derives the 0xB3 blanking bytes from the
+-- active mode. Without it, generated modes scan at the wrong porch.
